# issue-tracker — image-upload session token (FALLBACK)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory and fill in GH_SESSION_TOKEN:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored — it holds a credential, never commit it.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHEN YOU NEED THIS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Posting an image with `issue-tracker.sh comment <n> --image <file>` shells out
# to the `gh image` extension, which needs a GitHub *web session* cookie (the
# user-attachments upload flow has no API-token equivalent, so the `gh` CLI's
# own auth can't substitute).
#
# By default gh-image extracts that cookie from a local browser session — which
# works on a normal desktop. This file is the FALLBACK for environments where
# that extraction can't work, notably **WSL**: there gh-image's keyring backend
# is kwallet-bound and fails with `kwallet: password not found`, and the
# browser "Safe Storage" key needed to decrypt cookies isn't reachable from WSL.
#
# The skill only consults this file AFTER tokenless extraction fails, so on a
# machine where the browser path works you don't need a `.env` at all.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO GET THE TOKEN  (the github.com `user_session` cookie)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Chrome / Edge:
#   1. Log into github.com in the browser.
#   2. Open DevTools (F12) → Application tab.
#   3. Storage → Cookies → https://github.com
#   4. Find the row named `user_session`; copy its full Value.
#
# Firefox:
#   1. Log into github.com.
#   2. DevTools (F12) → Storage tab → Cookies → https://github.com
#   3. Copy the `user_session` Value.
#
# Notes:
#   - Use `user_session` (NOT `_gh_sess`, `__Host-…`, or `dotcom_user`).
#   - It's a session cookie: it grants access to your GitHub account, and it
#     expires / rotates when you log out or the session ages out. If uploads
#     start failing with an auth error, grab a fresh value.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERIFY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# After putting the value below into `.env`, confirm it's valid — this should
# print your GitHub username:
#
#     set -a; . .env; set +a
#     gh image check-token
#
# Then a normal upload works:
#
#     ./scripts/issue-tracker.sh comment 2 --body-file proof.md --image shot.png --yes
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COMMENT SIGNATURE  (who is posting)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every comment posted through this skill is signed with who you are, so issue
# threads stay attributable. Set your identity here (or pass --sign "<who>" per
# call, or export ISSUE_TRACKER_SIGNATURE). Examples:
#     ISSUE_TRACKER_SIGNATURE="Claude Code Opus 4.8"
#     ISSUE_TRACKER_SIGNATURE="Codex"
# Posting a comment with no signature configured is refused.
ISSUE_TRACKER_SIGNATURE=""

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paste the cookie value between the quotes (no surrounding spaces):
GH_SESSION_TOKEN=""
